1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Brazil only needed a draw… to win the World Cup. At home.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:09,900
July 16, 1950. The Maracanã, in Rio.

3
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:13,050
Around 200,000 people, by most accounts.

4
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,500
There was no final that year, just a group of 4.

5
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:20,000
Brazil had beaten Sweden 7–1, and Spain 6–1.

6
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:22,950
Some newspapers were already calling them champions.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,300
Just after half-time, Friaça scored. 1–0 Brazil.

8
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:30,400
Then Juan Schiaffino equalised for Uruguay.

9
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:33,200
1–1… still enough for Brazil.

10
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,900
With 11 minutes left, Alcides Ghiggia ran down the right…

11
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:41,200
…and shot low, inside the near post. 2–1 Uruguay.

12
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,800
The whole stadium… went silent.

13
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:47,400
Uruguay were world champions.

14
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:52,700
Brazil’s goalkeeper, Moacir Barbosa, was blamed for the rest of his life.

15
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:56,420
Biggest shock in World Cup history? Tell me in the comments.
